are driving your business.

00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:12.980
Now, if you're very, 
very early on,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.015
you want to see traction.

00:02:14.015 --> 00:02:15.266
But I think the reason I'm
jumping on this question

00:02:15.266 --> 00:02:17.088
is we now live in a 
culture where so many

00:02:17.088 --> 00:02:19.568
people think the following,

00:02:19.568 --> 00:02:21.167
which is they've been 
affected by Twitter,

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.222
Instagram, Facebook 
and Snapchat.

00:02:23.222 --> 00:02:25.964
If you get tens of 
millions of followers

00:02:25.964 --> 00:02:28.475
it doesn't matter that
you don't make money.

00:02:28.475 --> 00:02:30.305
You eventually 
become a billionaire.

00:02:30.305 --> 00:02:32.652
The problem is that works
for seven companies.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.332
That is not the norm.

00:02:34.332 --> 00:02:36.273
Most people try to,

00:02:36.273 --> 00:02:37.513
and this is what's 
going to happen

00:02:37.513 --> 00:02:38.916
over the next decade my friends,

00:02:38.916 --> 00:02:40.596
you will see, and over
the next three years,

00:02:40.596 --> 00:02:41.820
you will see an enormous
amount of companies

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.773
that went and tried to
get 10,000, 100,000,

00:02:44.773 --> 00:02:47.183
a million users,

00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:49.150
didn't get there,

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.934
weren't the hot product, 
the unicorn,

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.715
the once in a 
generation business.

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:56.877
The once in a 
generation business.

00:02:56.877 --> 00:02:58.965
And they ran out of money.

00:02:58.965 --> 00:03:00.760
And then you go out of business.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.190
So what I really want 
to ground this first

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.523
question in, in practicality.

00:03:05.523 --> 00:03:07.269
The only metric a business person

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:10.091
should be understanding
is their cash flow.

00:03:10.091 --> 00:03:11.722
Money in, money out.

00:03:11.722 --> 00:03:13.011
How do you build momentum?

00:03:13.011 --> 00:03:14.104
Is it heading in the right direction?

00:03:14.104 --> 00:03:18.827
I'm very proud that AJ
and I and the senior

00:03:18.827 --> 00:03:20.515
leadership that helped 
us along the way,

00:03:20.515 --> 00:03:22.098
we built an actual business here.

00:03:22.098 --> 00:03:24.088
VaynerMedia wasn't a valuation.

00:03:24.088 --> 00:03:26.045
VaynerMedia is 
revenue and profit.

00:03:26.045 --> 00:03:27.677
And I do think that 
we have gotten

00:03:27.677 --> 00:03:30.924
way too into 
users and mentions,

00:03:30.924 --> 00:03:32.408
and the one that 
bothers me the most,

00:03:32.408 --> 00:03:34.594
number of followers,

00:03:34.594 --> 00:03:36.193
and we've got away from
what are you doing?

00:03:36.193 --> 00:03:38.509
Do you know how many people
have come up to me and they're

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:39.863
like, yeah I'm struggling,

00:03:39.863 --> 00:03:43.518
and they're like this is
actually, DRock you were with me,

00:03:43.518 --> 00:03:45.817
it really hit me during
that one kid coming up to

00:03:45.817 --> 00:03:47.955
me in Colorado, and I don't
want to pick on the kid,

00:03:47.955 --> 00:03:52.078
but like everybody thinks
that amassing a following

00:03:52.078 --> 00:03:54.268
on social media is a business.

00:03:54.268 --> 00:03:57.677
Amassing a following on
social media is a platform

00:03:57.677 --> 00:04:00.927
for you to create 
a business on top of.

00:04:01.952 --> 00:04:05.590
A business, is a functioning
organization that

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.395
sells something that 
you make profit in

00:04:08.395 --> 00:04:10.786
so you can sustain 
that business and grow

00:04:10.786 --> 00:04:12.703
(snap)

00:04:15.479 --> 00:04:17.118
- [India] Joe.
- Joe.

00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:19.736
- [Voiceover] Joe asks, 
"You say to be ourselves 100%.

00:04:19.736 --> 00:04:22.152
"What if you have a troubled
past that you overcame?

00:04:22.152 --> 00:04:23.896
"Hide it or embrace it?"

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.376
- Well listen, I mean,
this is a tough question,

00:04:26.376 --> 00:04:27.550
it's something I think a lot about,

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.272
and I do think, and you've
been hearing from me,

00:04:29.272 --> 00:04:31.514
meditation, mental health,
I think the next frontier

00:04:31.514 --> 00:04:33.375
in the next 50 years of society,

00:04:33.375 --> 00:04:35.936
within the business
context, within society,

00:04:35.936 --> 00:04:37.080
gun control, 
all these other things,

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.035
we're going to be talking
more and more about the brain.

00:04:39.035 --> 00:04:41.270
Mental health, mental status.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.978
You know, there are
people in this world that

00:04:43.978 --> 00:04:45.234
come from such tough beginnings.

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.991
We talk a lot about
poverty, and opportunity,

00:04:47.991 --> 00:04:50.373
I think because we talk
about entrepreneurship.

00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:51.825
We don't talk, I don't talk,

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:55.106
a lot about you know, 
you were raped as a child,

00:04:55.106 --> 00:04:56.605
your parents were murdered.

00:04:56.605 --> 00:04:58.791
You know, some of these really
extreme, difficult things.

00:04:58.791 --> 00:05:01.961
I don't understand, or know,
what Joe's troubled past

00:05:01.961 --> 00:05:05.023
or if he's referring
for a friend or himself.

00:05:05.023 --> 00:05:06.801
I think we all have 
different versions of

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:07.878
a troubled past.

00:05:07.878 --> 00:05:09.413
Like some people 
would say I got bullied,

00:05:09.413 --> 00:05:10.327
and that was my troubled past.

00:05:10.327 --> 00:05:12.676
Others would say 
I was sexually molested,

00:05:12.676 --> 00:05:14.340
and that's my troubled,
like these all vary,

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.787
and so Joe what I would say
is I have no interest in

00:05:16.787 --> 00:05:18.875
sitting here on a high 
horse and deploying

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:21.485
generic blanket statements.

00:05:21.485 --> 00:05:22.872
I think that we should be,

00:05:22.872 --> 00:05:24.962
I do think that being
yourself 100% is something

00:05:24.962 --> 00:05:26.836
that people are attracted to.

00:05:26.836 --> 00:05:29.332
I think all of us, in
the same way that America

00:05:29.332 --> 00:05:31.177
actually doesn't hate the crime,

00:05:31.177 --> 00:05:33.182
they hate when you 
try to cover it up,

00:05:33.182 --> 00:05:35.238
because we know that you
are not being authentic,

00:05:35.238 --> 00:05:36.542
and you're trying to trick me,

00:05:36.542 --> 00:05:39.137
I think that's the same
reason we react so well

00:05:39.137 --> 00:05:40.425
to people that go very far,

00:05:40.425 --> 00:05:43.128
that own up to things,
that are super transparent,

00:05:43.128 --> 00:05:45.153
that are willing to go there,

00:05:45.153 --> 00:05:47.569
and so what I would 
say is, you know,

00:05:47.569 --> 00:05:50.112
you should challenge
yourself to go as far down

00:05:50.112 --> 00:05:52.579
that funnel as you can
because it is absolutely

00:05:52.579 --> 00:05:55.675
an attractive quality
that creates opportunity,

00:05:55.675 --> 00:05:57.637
happiness, business 
opportunities for one.

00:05:57.637 --> 00:06:01.406
However, I don't think you
have to air your dirty laundry,

00:06:01.406 --> 00:06:04.195
and I do think that 
there's a lot of help,

00:06:04.195 --> 00:06:06.300
and many other things
that people have to do

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.573
to be able to share things.

00:06:07.573 --> 00:06:09.893
I do not feel comfortable
sitting here saying

00:06:09.893 --> 00:06:11.456
yes, share your deepest, 
darkest things,

00:06:11.456 --> 00:06:14.229
because maybe you're
not emotionally ready.

00:06:14.229 --> 00:06:15.763
I don't know you on 
an individual basis.

00:06:15.763 --> 00:06:17.802
What I can tell you is
that everyday I try to push

00:06:17.802 --> 00:06:20.298
harder in exposing 
more of my thoughts,

00:06:20.298 --> 00:06:21.945
and exposing more of my truths,

00:06:21.945 --> 00:06:23.707
and exposing more 
of my weaknesses,

00:06:23.707 --> 00:06:26.823
and exposing more of my scars,

00:06:26.823 --> 00:06:28.568
and it's a struggle for me,

00:06:28.568 --> 00:06:31.211
because you guys have seen
over the last DailyVee's

00:06:31.211 --> 00:06:35.893
I don't spend a lot of time
on my weaknesses or my past.

00:06:35.893 --> 00:06:37.541
From yesterday's 
episode's first question,

00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:40.510
I don't hold grudges, 
I don't have a shit list.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.614
It's because I just don't
believe in containing

00:06:42.614 --> 00:06:46.163
negativities, and so
the only reason at this

00:06:46.163 --> 00:06:47.865
point in my life I'm trying
to think about

00:06:47.865 --> 00:06:49.496
my flaws or my struggles,

00:06:49.496 --> 00:06:51.910
is I want to give you, the
people who have decided to give

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.786
me your time, I feel a
sense of responsibility

00:06:53.786 --> 00:06:55.761
to all of you that are
giving me your time.

00:06:55.761 --> 00:06:56.755
How many people are 
on there right now?

00:06:56.755 --> 00:06:57.620
- [Voiceover] One point five.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.589
- For the 1500 of you right
now that are on Facebook Live,

00:07:00.589 --> 00:07:02.677
I feel a sense of responsibility
that in the middle

00:07:02.677 --> 00:07:04.374
of the day, or if you're in
Europe, later in the day.

00:07:04.374 --> 00:07:06.912
The fact that right now
1500 of you could be doing

00:07:06.912 --> 00:07:08.136
something completely different,

00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:10.844
but I have been 
gifted your attention,

00:07:10.844 --> 00:07:12.116
which I think is the 
number one asset,

00:07:12.116 --> 00:07:13.943
I'm trying to challenge myself,

00:07:13.943 --> 00:07:16.472
I'm trying to challenge myself,

00:07:16.472 --> 00:07:19.278
to expose some of my weaknesses
and things of that nature,

00:07:19.278 --> 00:07:21.415
but it's a real struggle for me.

00:07:21.415 --> 00:07:24.009
You know, 
so I'm almost the reverse,

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:25.805
like I can't even 
begin to think about my

00:07:25.805 --> 00:07:27.663
tough upbringing 
or different things,

00:07:27.663 --> 00:07:29.604
like I don't think 
about the bad things.

00:07:29.604 --> 00:07:31.352
Like I think about them, 
I deal with them,

00:07:31.352 --> 00:07:33.226
they're a reality, 
I don't dwell on them,

00:07:33.226 --> 00:07:35.461
I spit them out and 
I move forward.

00:07:35.461 --> 00:07:37.712
I think this is a very
personal question Joe.

00:07:37.712 --> 00:07:38.987
I think it's like work/life balance.

00:07:38.987 --> 00:07:42.233
I don't have an interest
in sitting on this show

00:07:42.233 --> 00:07:43.992
trying to force 
somebody right now

00:07:43.992 --> 00:07:45.966
that had a very horrible
thing happen to them,

00:07:45.966 --> 00:07:47.875
and they're going to write a
blog post about it tomorrow,

00:07:47.875 --> 00:07:49.066
and they weren't 
emotionally ready,

00:07:49.066 --> 00:07:50.551
and they can't deal 
with the repercussions

00:07:50.551 --> 00:07:51.578
of putting it out there.

00:07:51.578 --> 00:07:52.475
That is not my place,

00:07:52.475 --> 00:07:54.678
but I will say that everybody,

00:07:54.678 --> 00:07:56.342
if you can get there,

00:07:56.342 --> 00:08:00.031
I think there's a lot
of healthiness to it.

00:08:00.031 --> 00:08:01.114
Thanks India.

00:08:02.256 --> 00:08:06.321
- [India] From Matthew, what
was it like to go around?

00:08:06.321 --> 00:08:08.396
